.\" hkdf-tree — deterministic hierarchical passphrase derivation
.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd August 2, 2026
.Dt HKDF-TREE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm hkdf-tree
.Nd deterministic hierarchical passphrase derivation from a master seed
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm derive
.Op Fl \-salt Ar salt
.Fl \-info Ar info
.Op Fl \-output-len Ar n
.Op Fl \-raw
.Nm
.Cm list
.Fl \-config Ar file
.Op Fl v , \-verbose
.Op Fl \-status Ar status
.Op Fl \-derivation Ar kind
.Nm
.Cm show
.Fl \-config Ar file
.Fl \-entry Ar info-string
.Op Fl \-newline
.Nm
.Cm report
.Fl \-config Ar file
.Fl \-output Ar file
.Op Fl \-title Ar title
.Op Fl \-subtitle Ar subtitle
.Op Fl \-fingerprint Ar fp
.Op Fl \-entry Ar info-string
.Op Fl \-status Ar status
.Op Fl \-derivation Ar kind
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
derives passphrases deterministically from a single high-entropy master
seed using HKDF-SHA256 (RFC 5869).
Each credential is identified by a hierarchical info-string of the form
.Pa <domain>/<realm>/<purpose>-v<N> ,
declared in a YAML inventory together with its encoding (Diceware,
alphanumeric, numeric, or base64).
The same seed, salt, and info-string always reproduce the same
passphrase; nothing derived is ever stored.
.Pp
Subcommands that derive
.Pq Cm derive , Cm show , Cm report
read the master seed as
.Em raw bytes
from standard input.
Hex-encoded seeds must be decoded first, for example with
.Ql xxd -r -p .
.Sh SUBCOMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm derive
Apply HKDF-SHA256 to the seed on stdin with
.Fl \-salt
and
.Fl \-info ,
and write
.Fl \-output-len
bytes (default 32) to stdout, hex-encoded unless
.Fl \-raw
is given.
This is the low-level primitive; it does not consult an inventory.
.It Cm list
Load and validate the inventory given by
.Fl \-config
and print one info-string per entry, deterministically sorted.
.Fl v
adds derivation kind, status, and encoding per line.
.Fl \-status
.Pq Ar active , retired , reserved
and
.Fl \-derivation
.Pq Ar hkdf , manual , service-generated
filter the listing and may be repeated.
.It Cm show
Derive and encode a single entry, looked up by
.Fl \-entry ,
and print the resulting passphrase to stdout without a trailing
newline (add one with
.Fl \-newline ) .
Entries with
.Ar manual
or
.Ar service-generated
derivation are refused.
.It Cm report
Generate a printable A4 PDF
.Pq Fl \-output ,
one card per inventory entry: a human-readable title (the purpose's
.Ic usage
text) next to a QR code, followed by info-string, encoding,
passphrase, paper-backup destinations, and notes.
The output file is created with mode 0600.
.Fl \-fingerprint
prints a short seed fingerprint on the cover page for
cross-verification against the paper backup.
.Pp
By default every entry is included.
.Fl \-entry
restricts the report to the given info-string and may be repeated;
.Fl \-status
and
.Fl \-derivation
filter as they do for
.Cm list ,
but apply only when
.Fl \-entry
is absent, so an explicitly named entry can never be dropped silently.
Selection happens
.Em before
derivation: passphrases of unselected entries are never computed and
therefore never reach the output file.
Reprinting one card thus exposes exactly that one secret.
An info-string that matches nothing is an error, and no file is written
\(em otherwise a typo would be indistinguishable from a successful run
until the passphrase is needed and cannot be reproduced.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A usage error (unknown flag, missing argument) exits with status 2.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Derive the low-level bytes for one entry:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
xxd -r -p seed.hex | hkdf-tree derive \e
    --salt acme-hkdf-v1 --info alice/laptop/fde-daily-v1
.Ed
.Pp
List all active HKDF-derived entries:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
hkdf-tree list --config ~/.config/hkdf-tree/inventory.yaml \e
    --status active --derivation hkdf -v
.Ed
.Pp
Reproduce one passphrase:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
hkdf-tree show --config inventory.yaml \e
    --entry alice/laptop/fde-daily-v1 --newline < seed.bin
.Ed
.Pp
Generate the paper-backup report:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
hkdf-tree report --config inventory.yaml \e
    --output /tmp/report.pdf --subtitle "$(date +%F)" < seed.bin
.Ed
.Pp
Reprint a single card, deriving nothing else:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
hkdf-tree report --config inventory.yaml \e
    --entry alice/laptop/fde-recovery-v1 \e
    --output /tmp/one.pdf < seed.bin
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr gpg 1 ,
RFC 5869
.Pp
Project documentation:
.Pa README.md ,
.Pa docs/
in the source repository.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Dr. Johannes Brügmann Aq Mt dr.johannes.bruegmann@gmail.com
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
The PDF report contains every derived passphrase in plaintext.
Write it to volatile storage (tmpfs), print on an offline printer,
and destroy the file afterwards; the tool never encrypts anything
itself.
The master seed should only be entered on trusted, preferably
air-gapped systems.
The inventory file contains no secrets, only structure and public
parameters (including the salt), and may be backed up freely.
